    "body": "## Summary\n- Added `AddAndConsumeDocumentsWithOpstamp` and `DeleteDocumentsWithOpstamp` methods that return operation stamps\n- Added `BatchAddAndDeleteDocumentsWithOpstamp` for performing both add and delete operations in a single commit\n- Temporarily disabled rollback functionality due to Tantivy bug #2666\n- Fixed Windows compilation issues\n- Fixed Rust warnings\n\n## Changes\n\n### New Methods\n1. **`AddAndConsumeDocumentsWithOpstamp`** - Returns opstamp after adding documents\n2. **`DeleteDocumentsWithOpstamp`** - Returns opstamp after deleting documents  \n3. **`BatchAddAndDeleteDocumentsWithOpstamp`** - Performs add and delete in single commit for better performance\n\n### Backward Compatibility\n- Original `AddAndConsumeDocuments` and `DeleteDocuments` methods maintained for backward compatibility\n- They now call the WithOpstamp variants internally but only return error\n\n### Performance Benefits\nThe batch operation method reduces I/O overhead by committing once instead of twice when both adding and deleting documents.\n\n### Temporary Workaround\nRollback is temporarily disabled in Rust code due to critical Tantivy bug. See comments in code referencing https://github.com/quickwit-oss/tantivy/issues/2666\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] All existing tests pass\n- [x] Added comprehensive tests for batch operations\n- [x] Tested add-only, delete-only, and combined operations\n- [x] Verified error handling",
